---
// src/pages/privacy.astro
// Change this import to match your site's base layout.
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const lastUpdated = 'November 3, 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | Barkhaus"
  description="How Barkhaus collects, uses, and protects information for animal rescues and the people they work with."
>
  <main class="legal">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

    <p>
      Barkhaus ("Barkhaus," "we," "us") provides software that helps animal rescues manage
      their animals, applications, volunteers, communications, and donations, available at
      <a href="https://www.barkhaus.io">barkhaus.io</a> and <a href="https://app.barkhaus.io">app.barkhaus.io</a>
      (together, the "Service"). This policy explains what information we collect, how we use
      it, and the choices you have.
    </p>

    <h2>1. Who this policy covers</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Rescue staff and volunteers</strong> who create an account and use the Barkhaus dashboard.</li>
      <li><strong>Visitors</strong> to barkhaus.io and to rescue websites powered by Barkhaus.</li>
      <li><strong>Adopters, applicants, fosters, volunteers, and donors</strong> who submit information through a rescue's Barkhaus-powered website or forms.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      For information submitted to a specific rescue, that rescue decides why and how the
      information is used and is responsible for it. Barkhaus processes that information on the
      rescue's behalf to operate the Service.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Information we collect</h2>
    <h3>Account information</h3>
    <p>
      When you sign up or sign in, we collect your name, email address, password (stored in
      hashed form), and your role and organization membership. If you choose "Continue with
      Google," we receive your Google account email address, name, and profile picture from
      Google.
    </p>

    <h3>Rescue and content data</h3>
    <p>
      Information that rescues and their users enter into Barkhaus, such as animal profiles and
      photos, adoption and foster applications, applicant contact details, messages, events,
      volunteer records, and website content and branding settings.
    </p>

    <h3>Donation information</h3>
    <p>
      Donations are processed by our payment provider, Stripe. Payment card details are
      collected and stored by Stripe and are never stored on Barkhaus servers. We receive
      limited information such as donor name, email, amount, and transaction status.
    </p>

    <h3>Usage and device information</h3>
    <p>
      We collect technical information such as IP address, browser type, device type, pages
      viewed, and referring pages. We use cookies and similar technologies, including Google
      Tag Manager and Google Analytics, to understand how the Service is used and to improve it.
    </p>

    <h3>Communications</h3>
    <p>
      If you contact us or sign up for updates, we keep the messages you send and your contact
      details so we can respond.
    </p>

    <h2>3. How we use information</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>To provide, operate, and secure the Service, including authentication and access control.</li>
      <li>To display rescue websites, animal listings, and process applications and donations.</li>
      <li>To provide optional features such as AI-assisted reply drafting for rescue staff.</li>
      <li>To send service-related messages such as account, security, and billing notices.</li>
      <li>To analyze usage, fix problems, and improve the Service.</li>
      <li>To prevent fraud and abuse and to comply with legal obligations.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We do not sell your personal information, and we do not use it for third-party advertising.</p>

    <h2>4. Sign in with Google and Google user data</h2>
    <p>
      Barkhaus uses Google Sign-In only to authenticate you. We request access to your basic
      Google profile: your email address, name, and profile picture. We use this information
      only to create and secure your Barkhaus account and to identify you within your
      organization. We do not access your Gmail, Drive, Calendar, contacts, or other Google
      data.
    </p>
    <p>
      Barkhaus's use and transfer of information received from Google APIs to any other app
      will adhere to the
      <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>,
      including the Limited Use requirements. You can revoke Barkhaus's access at any time in
      your <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions">Google Account permissions</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>5. How we share information</h2>
    <p>We share information only as described here:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>With the rescue you interact with.</strong> Information you submit through a rescue's site or forms goes to that rescue.</li>
      <li><strong>With service providers</strong> that help us run the Service and are bound to protect the data: Supabase (database and authentication), Vercel (hosting), Stripe (payments), Google (sign-in and analytics), and AI providers used for optional reply drafting.</li>
      <li><strong>For legal reasons,</strong> such as complying with law, enforcing our terms, or protecting rights, safety, and security.</li>
      <li><strong>In a business transfer,</strong> such as a merger or acquisition, with notice to affected users.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>6. Cookies and analytics</h2>
    <p>
      We use cookies and similar technologies to keep you signed in, remember preferences, and
      measure usage. You can control cookies through your browser settings and can opt out of
      Google Analytics with the
      <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout">Google Analytics Opt-out Browser Add-on</a>.
      Blocking some cookies may affect how the Service works.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Data retention</h2>
    <p>
      We keep information for as long as your account or your rescue's account is active and as
      needed to provide the Service. When an account is closed, we delete or de-identify its
      data within a reasonable period, except where we must keep it for legal, security, or
      backup purposes.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Security</h2>
    <p>
      We use industry-standard safeguards, including encryption in transit, access controls,
      and per-organization data separation. No system is perfectly secure, so we cannot
      guarantee absolute security.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Your choices and rights</h2>
    <p>
      You can access, correct, or delete your account information from within your account or by
      contacting us. Depending on where you live (for example, California), you may have
      additional rights to know, access, correct, delete, or restrict the use of your personal
      information, and not to be discriminated against for exercising those rights. If you are
      an adopter, applicant, or donor, contact the rescue you dealt with, or contact us and we
      will help route your request. To make a request, email
      <a href="mailto:hello@barkhaus.io">hello@barkhaus.io</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Children's privacy</h2>
    <p>
      The Service is not directed to children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect
      personal information from them. If you believe a child has given us information, contact
      us and we will delete it.
    </p>

    <h2>11. International users</h2>
    <p>
      Barkhaus is operated in the United States. If you use the Service from outside the U.S.,
      your information will be transferred to and processed in the U.S.
    </p>

    <h2>12. Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this policy from time to time. We will post the updated version here with a
      new "Last updated" date and, for material changes, notify account holders by email or in
      the app.
    </p>

    <h2>13. Contact us</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about this policy? Email <a href="mailto:hello@barkhaus.io">hello@barkhaus.io</a>.
    </p>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal {
    max-width: 760px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 4rem 1.5rem 6rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
  .legal h1 { margin-bottom: 0.25rem; }
  .legal h2 { margin-top: 2.5rem; }
  .legal h3 { margin-top: 1.5rem; }
  .legal .updated { opacity: 0.7; margin-bottom: 2rem; }
  .legal ul { padding-left: 1.25rem; }
  .legal li { margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
</style>
